Build the Windows installer on GitHub for every overlay push

Purpose:
Always have an installable Windows build of the current overlay without
building locally: every push to `overlay` (git overlay-publish) builds
the NSIS installer and publishes it at a fixed URL.

Approach:
- .github/workflows/overlay-windows-build.yml at the repo root (only root
  workflows run in the monorepo), on windows-latest, for pushes to
  `overlay` and manual runs.
- No versioning: one rolling prerelease, tag `overlay-build`. Each run
  deletes it (and the tag) and recreates it at the built commit, with
  the installer as Gingko-Writer-Setup.exe, so the download link
  releases/download/overlay-build/Gingko-Writer-Setup.exe never changes.
- `bun install --ignore-scripts` skips the Electron download and
  node-pty's native build, which only the web/Electron tooling needs;
  Elm 0.19.1 is therefore fetched as a standalone binary (ELM_BINARY)
  instead of via the npm package's install script.
- Rust (Swatinem/rust-cache) and Elm packages (elm-home) are cached; a
  newer push cancels a running build.

Constraints:
- Windows NSIS installer only; unsigned (SmartScreen warns on first run).
- Doesn't touch upstream's workflows (web-deploy.yml runs only on
  master, on upstream's self-hosted runner).

